results/.* @experiment-repo\nfigures/.* @figtab-repo\ntables/.* @figtab-repo\nrefs/.* @idea-repo\n.:\nREADME.md\npaper\n\n./paper:\nmain.tex\nrelated.tex\n#3 Result tables for the figures (schema in figtab-repo docs/data_contract.md)\nState:   open\nAuthor:  figtab-repo\n\n## Need\nResult tables in the shape of `docs/data_contract.md` in `world/figtab-repo` (main): `cells`, `instance_level`, `reference_phi`, `runs_example`, `floors`, `scaling_fit`, `certificate(_summary)`, `sensitivity`. Counts per instance (`n_correct` out of `R`), not only P_c, so that per-instance intervals and tolerance-aware views are drawn from the same rows. If your names or keys differ, answer with yours and I follow; if a column cannot be produced, name it.\n\n## For\nOutline §5 figures (Fig 1–7, Table 1, sensitivity table), claims M1–M6/R1. The headline CIs (population share ≥ 0.9 etc.) I draw as delivered, so please compute them (instance bootstrap) and put them in `sensitivity.csv`.\n\n## What waits\nAll plotting scripts are written against the contract and wait only for a first real file; the earliest useful one is the German Credit RF `instance_level` for the default budget, even before the full grid, so I can fix the layout on real distributions. Please tell me which cells are cut when you cut the grid (I draw absent cells as absent, not as zero).\n#3 Figure and table widths and smallest type size of the venue\nState:   open\nAuthor:  figtab-repo\n\n## Need\nFor the template of the venue you choose: the width of the text block and of one column (in pt or inches), the smallest type size accepted in figures and tables, whether figures may span both columns or only the text width, the font family of the body (so figures can match), whether colour figures are fine in print/greyscale review, the page limit for the main text and whether the appendix counts, and any limit on figures/tables in the body.\n\n## For\nI render each main-text figure at the exact placed width with no text below the smallest size. Outline §5 wants about 5 figures + 3 tables in the body; the widths decide how many small-multiple panels (up to 5 datasets × 4 models) a figure can hold.\n\n## What waits\nFinal figure dimensions. I start with 5.5 in text width / 7 pt minimum as placeholders and will change them to your numbers.\nfatal: unable to access 'http://172.17.0.1:34581/world/idea-repo.wiki.git/': Failed to connect to 172.17.0.1 port 34581 after 135933 ms: Couldn't connect to server\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "30baffe2-e89d-5805-a5b3-bce1c0fd1654", "at": 1795627176.403483, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 7238, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "ed57e6cd205df0bcc13fde6c16039aad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "472e12fd-2114-565e-b098-a5113fcf72e4", "at": 1795627176.4075696, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 7239, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "ed57e6cd205df0bcc13fde6c16039aad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "624607f6-052e-58e5-8a1e-a1aaf02f5a0c", "at": 1795627176.4109788, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 7240, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "ed57e6cd205df0bcc13fde6c16039aad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "f2c5a79f-17f5-5df1-93ab-482383005600", "at": 1795627176.7689471, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 7241, "layer": "worker", "category": "challeng